[Cost & Token Analysis] Aggregate total input tokens and output tokens and request count grouped by model (model).
==============================================================================
Analyzing context
Retrieved context for 26 tables.
Running a query
SELECT COALESCE(model_version, 'unknown') AS model,
       COUNT(*) AS request_count,
       SUM(usage_prompt_tokens) AS total_input_tokens,
       SUM(usage_completion_tokens) AS total_output_tokens,
       SUM(usage_total_tokens) AS total_tokens
FROM `antigravity-503007.agent_telemetry.v_llm_response`
WHERE timestamp >= TIMESTAMP_SUB(TIMESTAMP '2026-09-11 04:46:02 UTC', INTERVAL 7 DAY)
GROUP BY model
ORDER BY request_count DESC
Query execution completed
Query returned 1 row in 1.71s.
I assumed a default time window of the last 7 days to optimize partition pruning on the telemetry table. Let me know if you would like to analyze a different timeframe.
